    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-l/q7-question-1.svg\" alt=\"dy dx = ( + ) x &gt; y &gt; x y y 1 , 0 , 0 Show that the solution of the above differential equation subject to the boundary 1 1 condition y = at x = , is given by 2 3 x = − y . ( 11 ) 1 x\" style=\"--madas-width:590.8px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-l/q7-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"From x dy/dx = y(y + 1), move the differentials to get x dy = y(y + 1) dx, hence dy/[y(y + 1)] = dx/x. Set 1/[y(y + 1)] = A/y + B/(y + 1). Clearing the denominator gives 1 = A(y + 1) + By. With y = 0 obtain A = 1, and with y = −1 obtain 1 = −B, so B = −1. Separate variables and integrate: Z dx Z 1 1   y  y − dy = x , = ln x + C [M1] [A1] ln y + 1 y + 1 since integration gives ln |y| −ln |y + 1| = ln |x| + C. Exponentiating gives y/(y + 1) = kx, where k = eC, using x, y &gt; 0. [M1] [A1] At x = 1 3, y = 1 2 the ratio y/(y + 1) equals 1/3, giving 1/3 = k/3, hence k = 1, so C = 0. [M1] [A1] Thus y/(y + 1) = x, [M1] [A1] hence y = (y + 1)x = xy + x, y −xy = x, y(1 −x) = x, giving y = x/(1 −x) [M1] [A1] on 0 &lt; x &lt; 1. [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 7 is 11 marks.</p>"
    ],
